{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To the house of Pharaoh, saying.</b> Meaning, that they should also convey to Pharaoh the manner in which he spoke to them, for he prefaced his appeal to them in this manner and thereby inclined his favor in Pharaoh's eyes. Or it may be said along the lines of what they of blessed memory stated (Yoma 4a): From where do we derive that one may not say to his fellow something he was told [in confidence] until the other explicitly tells him, 'Say it'? As it is written, ״וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳״ and so forth, ״לֵאמֹר״ (Leviticus 1:1). Likewise in our verse, the implication of לֵאמֹר is that they should convey the content of the address that he spoke to them in this manner to the house of Pharaoh." "<b>If now I have found.</b> Meaning, ״נָא״ is an expression of entreaty and of timing, for there was no opportunity to show Joseph love and favor except at this particular time and moment, for they had no need for anything." "<b>Speak now.</b> Meaning, now, immediately, for he was afraid to delay the fulfillment of the oath." "<b>In the ears of Pharaoh, saying.</b> The reason he said <b>לֵאמֹר</b> is that he intended that they too, of their own accord, would speak to persuade Pharaoh regarding the matter, so that he would do it."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:17.822430820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}